# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EDITOR / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEPENDENCIES — installed, never committed. Both are rebuilt on deploy from
# their lockfiles, and between them they are ~500MB of other people's code.
# (craft/vendor is also ignored by craft/.gitignore; kept here so the root file
# tells the whole story.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules
craft/vendor

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS — the reason to read this file before the first commit.
#
# craft/.env holds the Anthropic API key, the Spotify client secret and refresh
# token, and the database credentials. craft/.env.example is the committed
# version: keys with no values. (Also in craft/.gitignore.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
craft/.env
.ddev/.env.web

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CRAFT RUNTIME — logs, caches, compiled templates, database backups.
#
# Ignored for size (224MB) and for content: storage/logs/phperrors.log dumps the
# entire environment on a fatal error, API key included, so committing this
# directory would publish the secrets that craft/.env carefully does not.
#
# Craft recreates everything in here on demand. Nothing in it is source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
craft/storage/*
!craft/storage/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATED WEBROOT
#
# cpresources  — control panel assets Craft republishes itself
# dist         — the Vite build; built on the server at deploy time
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
public/cpresources/*
!public/cpresources/.gitkeep
public/dist

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UPLOADED ASSETS — 292MB of photography, and NOT source code.
#
# These are content, not code: they arrive through the control panel, and on
# Forge they live in a `shared/assets` directory symlinked into each release,
# which is what lets generated image transforms survive a deploy. Committing
# them would put the same files under two systems of record and make every
# clone a 300MB download.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, worth knowing: a fresh server starts with no images. Copy them up
# once, out of band (rsync to the shared directory), not through git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
public/assets
